{#- testing/remote_harness/templates/lme-seed-installed-set-gate.sh.j2 -- the INSTALLED-SET GATE fragment EXPORT
    (codex-tick313 transfer-pass-macro-join; path = the resolved controller.bootstrap.seed_fragments.installed_set_gate_rel,
    C1-registered). The same export pattern as the launch-params export (lme-seed-launch-params.json.j2): a thin call of
    the canonical macros, no second implementation. It emits, from macros/controller_seed.j2:
      refusal_fn(lme_seed_bs.refusals)                -- the seed's ONE lme_refuse shell function
      installed_set_gate(lme_seed_bs, lme_seed_lock)  -- the SAME text install_venv embeds in the production seed
    Inputs (declarations, never extra-vars of desired state; the renderer passes the RESOLVED values, no raw-profile
    reload, no second merge): lme_seed_bs = resolved remote_harness.controller.bootstrap; lme_seed_lock = the file named
    by remote_harness.controller.lock_file_rel (the same value package.yml passes to the seed template).
    Shell contract of the rendered text: reads _inv; sets _bad, _brc and _norm; on refusal prints
    `REFUSED RH-SEED-IDENTITY-MISMATCH <reason>` on stderr and exits with bs.refusals.RH-SEED-IDENTITY-MISMATCH.
    Run it under the seed's base_env (LC_ALL: the freeze-line grep uses bracket ranges). Rendered only through the
    template lookup (G's fixtures); nothing in production executes it; NOT a bundle member.
    Import: the declared relationship of the two profile paths (macros_rel relative to the directory of
    installed_set_gate_rel), as the launch-params export. No trailing newline in this file, so the rendered export
    carries none on either toolchain. -#}
{%- import lme_seed_bs.macros_rel | relpath(lme_seed_bs.seed_fragments.installed_set_gate_rel | dirname) as m -%}
{{ m.refusal_fn(lme_seed_bs.refusals) }}
{{ m.installed_set_gate(lme_seed_bs, lme_seed_lock) }}